From 2848f03f94b8605cdbebfe4de28e759103f7a76b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:58:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: whole functions, property access and doubles
 in the 68k template JIT (J4)

- Whole functions: op_enter runs a CodeBlock's code from its next
  instruction when it has some, and counts calls towards compiling it; the
  replace slow path (reached from calls and returns) compiles it instead of
  giving up on the CodeBlock. Before, only loops reached the JIT, and a
  function that returned often stopped its own loops from being compiled.
- Property access: get_by_id and put_by_id get their own code for sites
  whose interpreter cache holds an own property (a replace, for puts). The
  code reads the cache as it runs, so the garbage collector clearing it or
  the slow path changing it stays safe; storing a cell takes the slow path
  unless the object needs no write barrier.
- Doubles: add, sub, mul and the compare-and-jumps work on the FPU when an
  operand is not an int32 or an int32 result overflows, out of line, before
  the slow path; a double constant operand gets the FPU code inline.
  fdadd/fdsub/fdmul round once to double, as JavaScript asks; the
  interpreter's double arithmetic now uses the same instructions
  (fdadd/fdsub/fdmul/fddiv/fdsqrt), so both give the same results. 68040
  and up.

useM68KPropertyFastPaths (default true) turns the property code off.
